    "family_reading": {
        "text": "Amazon Nova is an API only family, so no version publishes open weights and self hosting is not an option. Across the 5 versions, context windows run from 128000 to 1000000 tokens, and only 1 version supports reasoning. Inputs can include file, image, text and video, while output is text only. The spread is wide in cost and capability. Nova Micro and Nova Lite are the cheap tiers, at $0.04 and $0.06 per million input tokens, but both cap output at 5120 tokens. Nova Premier 1.0 costs $2.5 input and $12.5 output, with a 1000000 token context and 32000 output limit. Nova 2 Lite is the reasoning option, at $0.3 input and $2.5 output, with 65535 output tokens. The family suits long document, image and video understanding at low cost, while heavy output and reasoning work is limited to specific tiers.",
